From f6e79ab83196320ff2e1f3cf6d3e0c93840b3873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:56:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/23] WIP mmb: on-the-fly Q5_K and Q6_K dequant (WTYPE 6/7)
 for dense + routed/GLU

- mmb_dq_row_q5k (176 B super-block, affine + qh 5th bit)
- mmb_dq_row_q6k (210 B super-block, int8 per-16 scales, 6-bit q-32)
- Q5_K/Q6_K in supported_mm/_mmid/_glu + _will_take; Q6_K no longer needs the
  6 GiB bf16 shadow (on-the-fly now)
- Qwen3.6-35B-A3B UD-Q5_K_M: pp2048 2045->2303 (+12.6%), pp8192 1918->2141 (+11.7%)
- Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q6_K: pp2048 2129->2143 (+0.7%), pp8192 1975->2012 (+1.9%)
- PPL parity on both (14.435->14.391, 14.368->14.330)
